    {
      "id": "chromatin_reference",
      "title": "Candidates within 21,529 gene windows",
      "caption": "Figure 7. Five candidates within a broader H3K27me3 reference. [4] (A-D) WT versus EZH2 Y641F signal across 21,529 complete protein-coding gene windows. Rows retain both WT assignments; columns compare fresh and day-four Tregs. (E) Log2(gain/WT) window-mean ratios on a shared scale. Windows span the annotated outer 5-prime boundary +/-5 kb (GRCm38.78); 490 of 22,019 eligible windows lacked complete coverage. Insets retain every window, including values outside the enlarged main views. Aggregate tracks do not supply biological replication; no new normalization or significance test was applied.",
